Formatting is as specified: Arial 11pt body, 14/12/11pt bold headings, title page, TOC field on page 2, page breaks between modules, footer `BE-CCG-001 v1.0 | Mercans Compliance Regulations Team | 2026`.

**Questions marked "Not Applicable": none.** Every question got a substantive answer. The two that came closest, and how they were handled instead:
- *Mandatory military service leave* — answered "No", with the reason (compulsory service suspended by the Law of 31 December 1992) rather than a bare N/A.
- *Employee with a student loan* (Module 12) — Belgium has no payroll student-loan mechanism, so the example states that explicitly and substitutes a full wage-garnishment worked example under Judicial Code Art. 1409.

**Scope manifest S3 compliance verified programmatically:** `descoping_reason` (not `reason`) on all 7 out-of-scope filings, `client_impact` on all of them, `integrations.inbound` as an array of 12 objects, `product_mapping_required` boolean on all 10 in-scope filings, and F1–F22 in `known_failure_patterns_to_check`. Five filings are descoped as **HR-scope** per C1/F19 (social balance sheet, diversity reporting, occupational health, work rules deposit, single permit).

**Research notes worth flagging.** Two figures would have been wrong if taken from search summaries. Secondary sources returned assessment-year-2025 tax brackets (15,820/27,920/48,320) labelled as 2026; the FPS Finance page gives income year 2026 as **16,720 / 29,510 / 51,070**, allowance **EUR 11,180**. And the 1 April 2026 minimum wage was reported as both 2,189.81 and 2,189.91 — the first is correct, proven by 2,189.81 × 1.02 = 2,233.61, the published 1 August figure. Both are logged as new reusable controls **L4** and **L5** in `shared/CCG-Playbook-Learnings.md`, and `BE-COVERAGE.md` has a dated changelog entry recording Stage 1 completion and the charter re-read (no drift found).

**One open risk for the record:** there are still no official source PDFs under `00-official-sources/`. The guide is built on FPS Finance, NSSO administrative instructions 2026/2 and FPS Employment web sources. That is captured in `known_limitations` in the manifest — the Annex III 2026 rules text, the NSSO instructions and the DmfA/Belcotax schemas should be obtained before any artefact is treated as final.
